      "prompt_version": "hub-chat:machine_selected",
      "retrieval_version": "oem_corpus_bm25",
      "answer_text": "\u26a0\ufe0f No page of the Allen-Bradley SLC 5/03 manual matched this question. The closest match is a related manual (Rockwell Automation CompactLogix, Rockwell Automation ControlLogix). Anything taken from it may differ on your SLC 5/03 \u2014 confirm them in your SLC 5/03 manual before you act.\n\nThe PLC stops communicating because the USR\u2011N540 is a transparent RS\u2011485\u2011to\u2011Ethernet converter and does not provide the DH\u2011485 protocol handling that the SLC\u202f5/03 expects on its DH\u2011485 network [1].  \n\nWith the drive isolated, locked out and the DH\u2011485 bus verified at 0\u202fV, first verify that the converter is configured (or capable) to speak the DH\u2011485 protocol or replace it with a DH\u2011485\u2011aware interface, and confirm the PLC\u2019s serial port is still set for DH\u2011485 communication as required by the built\u2011in serial port configuration [1].",
      "answer_status": "answered",
      "citations": [
